                <pb facs="0623" n="1357" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1357"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 695.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barnum to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harpoot</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Allen, Browne, Wheeler, ladies’ and five garden houses destroyed, also chapel,
                    boarding hall, Girls’ Theological Seminary building, $44,000; personal, $33,000;
                    stock and apparatus, $11,000; total, $88,000. Buildings set on fire separately
                    by Koords and citizens in presence of soldiers. No Armenian rioters. One hundred
                    soldiers quartered on premises now. Confidence weak.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnum.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
